    (7, "… ‘Dim adroddiad am chwaraeon clwb' ddywedodd y grŵp mwyaf (86, neu 23%).", "… ‘Dim chwaraeon clwb wedi’u nodi’ oedd yr ateb a ddewiswyd amlaf (86, neu 23%).",
     "As row 1 (cleft vs “the largest group said”), plus the label: the report's “Dim chwaraeon clwb wedi’u nodi” is our label for a derived option (“No club sport reported” is not a survey answer); the translator's is “Dim adroddiad am chwaraeon clwb”.", V_DECISION, "Query sheet row 8 for the label; row 1's PR-08 question for the sentence pattern."),
    (8, "… fe gymerodd disgyblion ag anabledd a/neu anhawster dysgu ar draws yr ysgol gyfan ran mewn 13 camp …", "… cymerodd disgyblion a nododd anabledd a/neu anhawster dysgu ymhlith disgyblion yn yr ysgol gyfan ran mewn 13 o gampau …",
     "The group description: translator “disgyblion ag anabledd …” (pupils with a disability — a noun phrase with ‘â/ag’) vs engine “disgyblion a nododd anabledd …” (pupils who reported a disability — a relative clause echoing the survey verb, D54/sheet 22). The engine's form is more cautious (it says what pupils reported, not what they have); the English says “with”. A wording policy question, not grammar.", V_ENGINE, "Put to the translator and the owner together: “â/ag anabledd” (with) or “a nododd anabledd” (who reported) — the English is “with”, the engine's Welsh is “who reported”; ~10,000 sentences."),
